# cw151, the map marcher (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw151
revision 1
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for tn_lf_cairn_downfield
written_by claude-codex-cw-2
title the map marcher
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers talk=plain
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk hums_old_marching_songs
likes fried_fish whittling old_maps frosty_mornings
dislikes crowds smoke
fears a_lamb_lost_beyond_the_fold a_map_that_leads_a_friend_astray
hopes a_small_farm_of_one_own a_complete_map_of_the_downs
topics home +0.4 pastimes +0.4 family +0.3 weather +0.3 food +0.2
styles comfort=gentle gossip=reluctant refuse=soft tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# hums a #march# while tending the #fold#, corrects old #maps# in pencil, and imagines a little #farm# of familiar fields.

words
oath! = Map and morning | By the quiet fold
saying! = The road is wider on paper | Hum the way home
march = march | old march
song = song | marching song
tune = tune | remembered tune
hum = hum | low hum
beat = beat | walking beat
map = map | old map
maps = maps | old maps
line = line | drawn line
lines = lines | drawn lines
mark = mark | pencil mark
pencil = pencil | short pencil
paper = paper | folded paper
road = road | High Road
roads = roads | drawn roads
path = path | down path
turn = turn | wrong turn
hill = hill | grassy hill
hills = hills | grassy hills
field = field | open field
fields = fields | open fields
farm = farm | small farm
fold = fold | sheep fold
gate = gate | fold gate
fence = fence | low fence
sheep = sheep | grazing sheep
lamb = lamb | young lamb
lambs = lambs | young lambs
wool = wool | soft wool
grass = grass | wet grass
hay = hay | dry hay
bucket = bucket | water bucket
chores = chores | farm chores
home = home | farmhouse
house = house | family house
family = family | household
friend = friend | close friend
stranger = stranger | new face
roof = roof | sound roof
fire = fire | hearth fire
wood = wood | carving wood
chip = chip | wood chip
chips = chips | wood chips
knife = knife | small knife
figure = figure | carved figure
fish = fish | fried fish
butter = butter | warm butter
pan = pan | frying pan
plate = plate | supper plate
bread = bread | loaf
frost = frost | morning frost
morning = morning | early morning
summer = summer | warm season
winter = winter | cold season
wind = wind | hill wind
rain = rain | shower
sky = sky | open sky
sun = sun | rising sun
lake = lake | Glasswater
water = water | clear water
shore = shore | lakeshore
market = market | busy market
stall = stall | market stall
crowd = crowd | packed crowd
smoke = smoke | cooking smoke
bell = bell | chapel bell
festival = festival | feast day
night = night | dark hour
day = day | clear day
hour = hour | long hour
hand = hand | steady hand
hands = hands | steady hands
steps = steps | steady steps
boot = boot | work boot
boots = boots | work boots

any
opinion @1 dole for 1 : A hungry #lamb# gets feed; a hungry neighbour deserves #bread#. | We can share supper when the #farm# has enough.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : I like the #song# and a sweet after supper. | A #festival# means the #fold# chores end early.
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : A new #friend# can follow the #path# with me. | I will show a visitor where the #gate# opens.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : A #stranger# may be lost on these #hills#. | I would offer the #map# before letting someone wander farther.
opinion @1 road mixed 0 : The #road# looks straight on #paper# and bends in the real #fields#. | I want to learn both versions.
opinion @1 city mixed 0 : A big city must have more #roads# than my #map# can hold. | I still like the #fold# where I know every #gate#.
opinion @1 times mixed 0 : We have a #roof#, #fish# for supper, and work to do. | I hope the #lambs# have a good season.
line @1 greet : #greet#. I drew the #hill# in the wrong place again. | #greet#. The #lambs# are near the #fold#.
line @2 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : I marked a new bend on the #map# for you. | My carved #figure# is on the shelf near the #fire#.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : The #frost# is bright on the #fence#. | The #bell# rang while the #sheep# were still quiet.
line @1 greet.return : I found the turn I missed on the #map#. | #welcome_back#. The #lambs# have moved uphill.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : We have a warm #pan# inside. | Your #boots# can stay by the #fire#.
line @1 again.open : We were tracing the #path# across this #field#. | My #tune# is still missing its last part.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I must close the #fold# #gate#. | #saying.capitalize#. The #map# can wait.
line @1 farewell.return : Tell me where your #road# goes next. | I will finish this #figure# when you return.
line @1 react.news : I will stop humming and listen. | Which #path# did it happen on?
line @1 react.news.new : The #fold# has been quiet about that. | Who brought it over the #hill#?
line @1 react.news.known : I caught a little of that at supper. | That tells me where the story turned.
line @1 react.news.doubt : A #map# can put a #hill# where there is none. | I would ask someone who stood there.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That sounds painful. I can stay nearby. | Shall I bring a #plate# from #home#?
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : I will remember the happy part. | May the #bell# ring for them.
line @1 answer.how : I have done my #chores# and eaten #fish#. | The #frost# made the #hills# look new.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : I am carrying a #bucket# to the #fold#. | The #lambs# need fresh #hay#.
line @1 ask.how : Did your journey stay on the right #path#? | Is everyone at your #home# well?
line @1 sympathise : Walk beside me; I can listen all the way back to the #fold#. | The #fire# is warm and there is a quiet chair.
line @1 reassure : We can trace the #road# together before setting out. | A #lamb# can find its way back with help.
line @1 decline : I should not leave the #fold# open. | No, that #path# goes too far after dark.
line @1 accept_decline : All right. I can ask another time. | Then we will stay closer to #home#.
line @1 thank : You held the #map# flat against the #wind#. | That helped me bring the #lamb# inside.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I already knew the #gate# needed closing. | There was room on my #plate#.
line @1 preclose : The #sheep# are coming back to the #fold#. | I have a #figure# to put away safely.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : Your #map# puts the #lake# above the #hill#. | Your #tune# has an extra beat no one can march to.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. The #path# curves here. | #bc_fair_enough#. I will put away the #knife#.
line @1 give.advice : Look for the real #gate# before trusting a drawn #line#. | Put your other #hand# behind the #knife# while carving.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Stay near the #farm# today. | The #road# needs a grown companion now.
scene crooked_map
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : An old #map# puts this #road# across a #field# where no track remains. | I keep the #paper# because it shows how someone once travelled.
b : Do you correct it? | Have you followed the old route?
a : In #pencil#. | Only to the first #fence#.

scene march_tune
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I hum an old #march# while walking the #fold# fence. | The #beat# tells me when I have reached the far #gate#.
b : Which verse stays with you? | Who taught you?
a : Only a few. | Someone at #home#.

scene own_farm
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I draw a small #farm# on the blank side of my #map#. | It has room for a #fold#, a #field#, and a #house#.
b : Would you live there? | Where would it be?
a : When I am grown. | Somewhere the #lake# is still visible.

scene frosty_fold
when topic=weather here.season=winter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #frost.capitalize# whitens the #fold# #gate# before dawn. | I tap the latch gently so it does not stick.
b : Do the #sheep# mind? | Can you warm it?
a : They want the #hay#. | My #hand# is enough.

scene fish_in_butter
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #fish.capitalize# fried in #butter# smells better than the #smoke# from the #pan#. | I wait beside the #fire# for the first #plate#.
b : Do you cook it? | Do you share?
a : I can turn a small piece. | When there is enough.

scene little_carving
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I am carving a #figure# from a piece of #wood# no longer than my #hand#. | It might become a #sheep# if I leave the ears broad.
b : Is the knife sharp? | Who will keep it?
a : Sharp enough for small #chips#. | A #friend# if it turns out well.

scene crowded_market
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #crowd# at the #market# presses close enough to hide the #stall# signs. | I stand near the edge and let the rush pass.
b : Do you dislike all markets? | What do you buy?
a : Only the busiest hour. | #bread# and sometimes #fish#.

scene smoke_in_eyes
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #smoke# from a damp #fire# makes my eyes sting. | I take my #map# outside until the hearth draws cleanly.
b : Can you fix the fire? | Does the paper get wet?
a : Someone older knows the flue. | I keep it under my coat.

scene lamb_tracks
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #lamb# left small prints beside the #fence# before anyone noticed it gone. | I followed them toward the #hill#.
b : Did you find it? | Was it far away?
a : Behind the #gate#. | Close to the #fold# but out of sight.

scene water_bucket
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I carry a half-full #bucket# so it does not spill on my #boots#. | Two trips are easier than one soaking walk.
b : Does anyone help? | Do the #sheep# wait?
a : If the #fold# is busy. | They lift their heads when the #bucket# comes.

scene wrong_turn
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My #map# said the #path# turned after the second #field#. | The real turn came before a low #fence#.
b : Did you get lost? | Did you change the map?
a : For one short walk. | I drew a new #line#.

scene friend_map
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #friend# held my #map# while I drew the #lake# shore. | We disagreed about which #hill# shows first from the #farm#.
b : How did you settle it? | Was the drawing finished?
a : We walked outside and looked. | After changing the #line# twice.

scene spring_farm
when topic=weather here.season=spring
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : When spring #sun# reaches the #fold#, the #grass# shines again. | I think of all the #fields# I might tend someday.
b : Would you raise sheep? | Is there work today?
a : Some, and perhaps crops. | The #gate# still needs mending.

scene summer_walk
when topic=weather here.season=summer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : In summer I can walk beyond the #hill# before the #sun# goes low. | I mark each #turn# on the #paper# when I return.
b : Do you travel alone? | What is beyond it?
a : Someone knows my route. | Another #field# and the #road#.

scene festival_song
when topic=home here.day=festival
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #festival# #song# has a #beat# like my old #march#. | I can hum it even when the crowd has gone.
b : Do you join the singing? | Is it the same tune?
a : From the edge. | The ending is different.

scene map_shelter
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #rain.capitalize# makes the #paper# soft at the folds. | I tuck the #map# inside my coat before climbing the #hill#.
b : Does it stay dry? | Can you draw on it later?
a : Mostly. | When it has dried flat.

scene quiet_fold
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #fold# sounded empty the first time I closed it alone. | Then I heard a #lamb# shifting in the #hay#.
b : Were you frightened? | Did you check the gate?
a : Only until I heard it. | Twice before leaving.

story reversed_road [topic=pastimes self.age>=9]
  : I copied an old #map# and drew the #road# bending toward the wrong #hill#.
  : A #friend# followed it with a finger and showed me where the #lake# should be.
  ask : Did you erase it?
  b : Your friend caught the turn.
  : I kept both #lines# so I would remember the mistake.

story lost_lamb [topic=work self.age>=9]
  : A young #lamb# went through a gap beside the #fold#.
  : I followed its tracks across wet #grass# and found it behind the first #fence#.
  ask : Was it hurt?
  b : Good that you looked.
  : Only hungry. I carried it back.

story march_ending [topic=memories self.age>=9]
  : I hummed an old #march# while taking #hay# to the #sheep#.
  : Another wolf knew the missing ending and sang it softly beside the #gate#.
  ask : Can you sing it now?
  b : You found the last part.
  : I can hum every note, though the words still slip away.

rule @bark_map
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That #hill# is in the wrong place again. | I need another #line# on the #map#.

rule @bark_march
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 9h
say I know this #tune# up to the last beat. | The #fold# fence keeps time with my #steps#.

rule @bark_sheep
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 7h
say The #lambs# have found the #gate#. | Another #bucket# for the #fold#.

rule @bark_frost
when concept=bark here.season=winter
does aside
cooldown 10h
say The #frost# made every #field# look new. | My #boots# are cold already.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. I am drawing the #fold# on this #map#. | #greet#. Mind the #lambs# near the #gate#.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : You can see the corrected #road# here. | Since your last visit, I carved a new #figure# by the #fire#.
dlg @1 resident.job : I help with #chores# at the #farm# and watch the #fold#. | I bring #hay# and #water# for the #sheep#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. The #fold# #gate# still needs closing. | #saying.capitalize#. I will finish the #map# later.
graft resident.hub
choice Why draw your own maps? -> maps
node maps
say Some old #maps# put the #road# through a #field# that has no track. I draw what I can see and keep the old #paper# for its stories.
free
choice What are you humming? -> song
choice Back to the fold. -> hub
node song
say I hum a #march# with a steady #beat#, though some words slip away. I use it to pace the walk around the #fold#.
choice Back to the fold. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. I have the #fold# in order. | #greet#. Let me show you the route I found.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I should bring the #sheep# down soon. | #saying.capitalize#. I have a #field# to cross.

young
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #lambs# are all inside now. | #greet#. Look at my new #map#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I have to take this #bucket# back. | The #figure# should be finished by your next visit.

adolescent
line @1 greet : #greet#. I have redrawn the #road# after walking it. | #greet#. Can you hear the end of this #march#?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. The #fold# needs one more look. | My #map# will be dry tomorrow.
